### 🎯 Find First and Last Position of Element (LeetCode 34)

Find both boundaries — the **first index >= target** and the **last index <= target**.

```python
class Solution:
    def searchRange(self, nums, target):
        n = len(nums)
        if n == 0:
            return [-1, -1]

        # Find first index >= target
        left, right = -1, n
        while right > left + 1:
            mid = (left + right) // 2
            if nums[mid] >= target:
                right = mid
            else:
                left = mid
        first = right

        if first == n or nums[first] != target:
            return [-1, -1]

        # Find last index <= target
        left, right = -1, n
        while right > left + 1:
            mid = (left + right) // 2
            if nums[mid] > target:
                right = mid
            else:
                left = mid
        last = right - 1
        return [first, last]
```

🧩 *First and last True zone boundaries in one shot.*

